\f1\fs22 Sarah was discovering morning sickness had a sense of timing rivalled only by tax collectors and STD results. She\'92d just reached something like human equilibrium when her tablet erupted with Roderick Ashby-Prynne\'92s upgraded ringtone, now featuring subliminal messages about productivity and collaborative excellence.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93What fresh hell is this?\'94 Sarah answered wearily.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Sarah! My little truant!\'94 Ashby-Prynne\'92s voice oozed enthusiasm freshly harvested from a People and Culture workshop. \'93How\'92s the recovery progressing? Still glowing?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Like Chernobyl in a sundress,\'94 Sarah croaked.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Splendid! Listen, poppet, there\'92s been some workplace disruption in your absence. The men have lost their morning momentum entirely. Jenkins missed a deadline because, quote, \'91there was no incentive to go to the printer.\'92 Thompson claims he\'92s forgotten how to operate the coffee machine. Market confidence is wobbling.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah pressed a hand over her stomach, where Richard was apparently attempting to recreate the siege of Stalingrad. \'93Are you calling to check on my health, or is this the new empathy initiative?\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Health, productivity, team dynamics\'97they\'92re all interconnected, aren\'92t they? Speaking of which, Thornberry submitted his excellent VisiTrust penetration testing report this morning\'97very thorough, great initiative.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah blinked. \'93I filed that report last week.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Oh, Sarah. Credit where credit\'92s due, please. You should know just being a woman in this office doesn\'92t allow you to claim someone else\'92s work. The timestamp says today at 8:04.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I\'92m telling you he must have resubmitted my work.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Thornberry\'92s been very generous, attached your preliminary notes as supporting documentation, which shows real collaborative leadership. He\'92s up for the quarterly innovation prize.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah\'92s free hand clenched into a fist that could have crushed walnuts to a fine paste. \'93He\'92s stealing my work, Roderick.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Look, I imagine you\'92ve worked at other places where, from time to time, the fairer sex have been given the kind of preferential privilege of claiming a win, but I must stress that we frown on sexism of any kind here.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93I\'92m just standing up for myself.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93And that\'92s exactly the kind of sexist privilege we want to stamp out, Sarah. Look, I suppose we could persuade Thornberry to give you some credit, in an appendix, of course... ah, with a picture, perhaps one of you in that\'97\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Red dress,\'94 Sarah finished the sentence for him.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Excellent brand representation\'97exactly what you were hired for. Stakeholders are visual learners, after all.\'94 He wheezed an aristocratic laugh, like a bishop passing a kidney stone.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Roderick, I was in an explosion. I\'92m on medical leave.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Yes, yes\'97heroic stuff. But we\'92re implementing Project Positivity Enhancement next week. People and Culture are dispatching a photographer for ambient encouragement documentation. The analytics indicate your engagement scores peak during filing activities, particularly when accessing the lowest drawers in the filing cabinets. Quite inspiring for quarterly projections.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93It sounds like you expect inspiring projections daily.\'94 Sarah found herself staring at an Elvis guard through her window. He was methodically polishing his rifle while humming \'93Don\'92t Be Cruel,\'94 and somehow that felt considerably less surreal than this conversation.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Roderick chuckled. \'93Yes! That\'92s the spirit. With your restorative presence, poppet, I\'92m sure we could aim for the stars.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>Sarah shut her eyes against the preposterous Ashby-Prynne\'85\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'85which did nothing to stop him blathering. \'93The office ecosystem requires balance. Your presence. Monday would be ideal\'97professional attire, positive energy. Perhaps something in pastels? Market research suggests pastels increase client confidence by twelve percent.\'94\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>\'93Good night, Roderick,\'94 Sarah said and hung up.\
<$ScrKeepWithNextSplittable>She closed her eyes and practised her Monday smile. A rictus that was less bright-eyed and bushy-tailed, more planning which parts of the ridiculous Roderick she might feed to the office shredder. She decided he needed to go face-first, and he\'92d deserve it. He probably authored the original employee manual, \'93Grin and Bare It,\'94 and found the legal settlements the real thrill.
